{title: One More Cup Of Coffee}
{artist: Bob Dylan}
{key: Am}

{c: Verse 1}
Your [Am]breath is sweet your eyes are like,        [G]two jewels in the sky
Your [F]back is straight,        your hair is smooth on the
[E]pillow where you lie,        But [Am]I dont sense affection,
no, nor [G]gratitude nor love,        Your [F]loyalty is not to me,
but [E]to the stars above,        [F]One more cup of coffee for the [E]road
[F]One more cup of coffee fore I [E]go,        to the valley [Am]below
Your [Am]Daddy hes an outlaw and a,        [G]wanderer by trade
Hell [F]teach you how to pick and choose,        and [E]how to throw the blade
He [Am]oversees his kingdom so no,        [G]stranger will intrude
His [F]voice it trembles as he calls for,        [E]another plate of food
[F]One more cup of coffee for the [E]road,        [F]One more cup of coffee fore I [E]go,
to the valley [Am]below,        Your [Am]sister sees the future
[G]like your mother and yourself,        Youve [F]never learned to read or write,
theres [E]no books upon your shelf,        But your [Am]pleasure knows no limits,
your [G]voice is like a meadowlark,        But your [F]heart is like an ocean,
[E]mysterious and dark,        [F]One more cup of coffee for the [E]road
[F]One more cup of coffee fore I [E]go,        to the valley [Am]below
